cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Evidome: cross-species functional evidence reports for pathway and upstream-regulator analysis"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/BioinformaticSolutions/evidome"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23459120
    description: "Archived releases, all versions"
authors:
  - family-names: Jones
    given-names: Kenneth L.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-1289-4652"
    email: Ken.Jones@bioinformaticsolutions.com
abstract: >-
  Evidome turns a gene-level differential expression result from any species
  into a structured, self-describing functional evidence report: gene-set
  enrichment (Reactome, Gene Ontology, WikiPathways, MSigDB Hallmark; ORA and
  preranked GSEA) and upstream-regulator evidence (CollecTRI and OmniPath),
  with every gene -- given as an Ensembl ID, an NCBI GeneID or a symbol --
  mapped to its human ortholog through Ensembl Compara. The
  report is written for an AI agent to read and interpret, with a browser
  page and a workbook for people.
keywords:
  - pathway analysis
  - gene set enrichment
  - upstream regulator
  - orthology
  - differential expression

# No version here: Zenodo takes the version from the release's git tag, so
# this file never states a stale one. The DOI above is the concept DOI, which
# always resolves to the newest archived version.
